I saw that thread on R-Devel as well and was quite excited about it.  As Cameron mentioned, the tikzDevice uses a rather brutal hack that re-writes, the Sweave internals while Sweave is processing the Rnw file and it would be nice to drop this in favor of something that is officially supported.  However, Romain's patch hasn't been integrated into the R trunk yet.  I just bumped the R-devel thread with a request for a status update---if other people chimed in as well, it would help motivate R-Core to implement it.

